# Jarvis Core (Always-On)

## Stack & Ports
- HUD: Next.js `frontend/` on **:3000**
- API: FastAPI `backend/app/` on **127.0.0.1:8000**
- Hermes Gateway: **:8642** (shop work brain)
- Speech: Gemini TTS, voice Charon, `POST /api/tts` (no Voicebox, no browser speech)
- Gemini: Casual chat + vision + speech + overflow
- Ollama: Last resort fallback

## Data Paths
- Database: `<repo>/data/jarvis.db` (SQLite)
- Written files: `<repo>/exports/` **only**
- Hermes sessions: `<repo>/data/hermes_sessions.json`
- Memory/LanceDB: `<repo>/data/memory/`

## Architecture Invariants
- **One page, one substrate:** `JarvisRoot` (root layout) owns the only WebGL context; `/` is `Desk` — a landing overlay, then vertical sections (Monitor → Casual → Engineering). Rules: `frontend/22-scroll-substrate.mdc`. `OrchestratorShell` and `HudShell` are not the desk
- **Features plug in, base stays put:** new work goes in `frontend/src/features/<id>/` + `backend/app/features/<id>/`, importing Jarvis code only via `@/sdk`
- **Two state layers, never collapsed:**
  - `HudWorkspace`: `casual` | `monitor` | `engineering` (job of the screen)
  - `JarvisState` turn FSM: `IDLE` | `LISTENING` | `THINKING` | `SPEAKING` | `AWAITING_HITL` | `EXECUTING`
- **Turn ledger** (`turn_ledger_enabled`, default **off**) is future work — not load-bearing
- **Jobs are Hermes playbooks** under `backend/app/hermes/playbooks/`, not new agents

## Hard Rules
- **Tools own** mail, calendar, files, and **every number**. Model never invents prices, rates, dimensions, mail, or calendar facts. No source → ask.
- **Authorize (HITL) before any action that commits the business or destroys data:** outbound mail, calendar write, quote send, sheet write, CNC promote, broad memory wipe. Queue it; never claim it was done. (Read-only fetches, dev tooling, and connector reads do not need HITL. For exploratory code, drafts, and mock-ups, treat these as guidance — ask before doing something that might commit, not after refusing.)
- **Never commit:** `.env`, `data/`, `exports/`, tokens, customer drawings.

